480 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 315 0 R
/E (The development of voice-controlled technology has become an important part of modern electronics and embedded systems. Voice activation allows users to interact with electronic devices through spoken commands without requiring physical contact. Traditional voice recognition systems often depend on cloud servers to process audio data, which can introduce communication delays, require continuous internet connectivity, and raise privacy concerns. To overcome these limitations, a Low Latency and Efficient Voice Activator for Edge Devices provides a solution by processing voice commands directly on local hardware.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
481 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 315 0 R
/E (Edge computing is a technology that performs data processing near the source of data instead of sending it to a remote server. In this project, an edge device, such as an ESP32 or ESP32-S3 microcontroller, is used to capture audio signals, detect voice activation commands, and trigger specific actions. The system can be designed using a microphone, a microcontroller, and an output device such as an LED or OLED display to indicate successful voice detection.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
482 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 315 0 R
/E (The primary objective of this project is to reduce response time while maintaining efficient utilization of memory, processing power, and energy. By performing voice detection locally, the system minimizes network dependency and improves reliability. Lightweight algorithms and optimized signal-processing techniques can help the device recognize predefined keywords with limited computational resources. This approach is particularly useful for embedded applications where low power consumption and fast responses are essential.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
483 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 315 0 R
/E (The proposed system has potential applications in smart homes, industrial automation, assistive technologies, healthcare devices, and intelligent robotics. It can enable hands-free operation, improve accessibility, and support real-time control in environments where internet connectivity is limited or unavailable.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
484 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 315 0 R
/E (In conclusion, a low-latency and efficient voice activator for edge devices demonstrates how embedded systems and voice-processing technologies can be combined to develop responsive, reliable, and cost-effective solutions. The project focuses on achieving faster voice activation, reduced computational overhead, improved privacy, and efficient local processing, making it a promising approach for next-generation intelligent edge applications.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
