554 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 323 0 R
/E (Voice activation technology has developed significantly with advances in speech recognition, embedded systems, artificial intelligence, and edge computing. Early voice recognition systems relied on computers with high processing capabilities to identify spoken commands. These systems often required considerable computational resources and were not suitable for small, low-power embedded devices.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
555 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 323 0 R
/E (Later, cloud-based voice assistants introduced more advanced speech recognition capabilities. These systems process audio data on remote servers and provide responses to user commands. Although they offer improved recognition performance, they depend on internet connectivity and may experience delays due to network communication. They can also raise privacy concerns because voice data may be transmitted to external servers.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
556 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 323 0 R
/E (Recent research has focused on edge-based voice processing using microcontrollers and lightweight machine learning algorithms. Platforms such as ESP32 and ESP32-S3 support embedded applications that can perform predefined keyword detection locally. Techniques such as digital signal processing, feature extraction, and compact neural networks help reduce computational complexity and response time.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
557 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 323 0 R
/E (Existing studies demonstrate that local voice processing can improve responsiveness, reduce network dependency, and support privacy-conscious applications. However, challengesremain in achieving high detection accuracy under noisy conditions while maintaining low power consumption and limited memory usage.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
558 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 323 0 R
/E (Therefore, the proposed Low Latency and Efficient Voice Activator for Edge Devices project focuses on developing an affordable embedded system that detects predefined voice commands locally and provides fast responses with efficient resource utilization.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
